<figure id="S6.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:70%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span><span id="S6.T4.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Evaluation of Text-to-Image Generation on DPG <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hu et al., 2024</a>)</cite> Benchmark</span>. “Und.” and “Gen.” denote “understanding” and “generation”, respectively. We highlight the <span id="S6.T4.11" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;">best</span> and the <span id="S6.T4.12" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;">second</span> results. “<math id="S6.T4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\dagger" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>†</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\dagger</annotation></semantics></math>” means the MMaDA results are evaluated by ourselves.
</figcaption>
